// Added 2026-08-18. There is deliberately NO maxCodeComplexity override here.
//
// Pylance used to grey out ~60 names in agents/voice/realtime_worker.py as
// 'not accessed'. Every one was a false positive: pyright was refusing to
// analyse _oai_to_twilio at all —
//
//   'Code is too complex to analyze; reduce complexity by refactoring into
//    subroutines or reducing conditional code paths'
//
// — and once it gives up on a function it can no longer prove any local in it
// is read, nor see the calls that function makes, so module-level helpers used
// only from inside it were greyed too. Confirmed independently: an AST pass
// found ZERO assigned-but-never-read locals and ZERO unreferenced
// module-level names in that file.
//
// Raising maxCodeComplexity does NOT fix it. Tried 4096, 16384, 65536 and
// 262144 — the bail persisted at every value. The only fix is the one the
// message names, so _oai_to_twilio was split: 1,264 lines / 161 branch points
// down to 599 / 91, and the diagnostic cleared on its own.
//
// If it ever comes back, split the function again rather than adding a ceiling
// here. The setting would hide the warning while leaving the code unanalysed,
// and every recurring bug of that session — the barge-in pre-audio race, the
// six response.create sites, the dead-air condition, the audio_rms overwrite —
// lived in exactly that unanalysed region.
//
// A REAL // COMMENT, not a "//" KEY. Pyright reads JSONC, so the prose
// above is a comment; as a key it was an unrecognised setting and pyright
// said so on every single run — a warning printed by every green build is
// a warning nobody reads.
//
// `include` IS THE ONE LIST. CI runs bare `npx pyright`, so the set of
// checked paths lives here and nowhere else. It used to be duplicated as
// CLI arguments in the workflow, and the two had already drifted:
// check_refusals.py was in the workflow's list and missing from this one.
{
  "include": [
    "agents",
    "check_refusals.py",
    "core",
    "run_mockups.py",
    "run_twilio.py",
    "test_realtime_protocol.py"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "**/.*",
    "**/.venv",
    "**/node_modules",
    "**/__pycache__"
  ],
  "typeCheckingMode": "basic"
}
